# CODEOWNERS for <org>/tenant-a-gitops
#
# The second of two repositories (the machine repo). Kept separate from the
# workloads repo because ArgoCD reads this repo, and CI bots write rendered manifests
# to it. It is the one repo where automation holds credentials.
#
# In this monorepo its root is 3-tenant-repos/tenant-a/gitops-repo/; when the
# tree is extracted it becomes the real repository root unchanged
# (docs/adr/0010-tenant-repository-topology.md):
#
#   git subtree split \
#     --prefix=3-tenant-repos/tenant-a/gitops-repo -b tenant-a-gitops
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so the general rule goes first.

# The team owns its own workloads: per-env values.yaml and CI-rendered manifests.
*                                       @acme-corp/team-a

# The tenancy boundary and ArgoCD wiring are platform-owned. A team cannot widen its
# own AppProject, relax its NetworkPolicy, or repoint its ApplicationSet.
/platform/                              @acme-corp/platform-engineering

# Kyverno exceptions weaken a cluster-wide guardrail, so security signs those off.
/platform/tenancy/policy-exceptions.yaml   @acme-corp/security
